  "summary": "A Man'yō botanical garden is a Japanese form of botanical garden that attempts to contain every species and variety of plant mentioned in the Nara period Man'yōshū poetry anthology.",
  "description": "A Man'yō botanical garden is a Japanese form of botanical garden that attempts to contain every species and variety of plant mentioned in the Nara period Man'yōshū poetry anthology. It is somewhat similar to a Shakespeare garden in the English-speaking world.\n\nSpecific Man'yō gardens include:\n\nAkatsuka Botanical Garden\n\nFutagami Manyo Botanical Gardens\n\nMichinoku Mano-Manyo Botanical Garden\n\nManyo Botanical Garden, Nara",
